          "explanation": "Mere awareness is weak because biases operate by not feeling biased from the inside — you cannot 'notice' what doesn't feel wrong. A structural procedure, like forcing yourself through all six question categories including generating a real counterargument, works regardless of whether anything feels off, which is why it functions as genuine debiasing.",
